&lt;p&gt;PlanetScale is growing rapidly and reinventing the database space. Our database platform offers developers the fastest and most reliable Postgres and Vitess/MySQL databases, enabling businesses to efficiently handle data and workloads of all sizes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;PlanetScale is backed with over $100M in venture financing from top-tier VCs including a16z, Kleiner Perkins, SignalFire, and Insight Venture Partners. And we serve some of the most innovative companies in the world such as Block, Anysphere (Cursor), MyFitnessPal, Etsy, Kick, and thousands more. Our customers entrust us with what is often their most precious digital asset, their data, so the stakes couldn&#39;t be higher.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Brand Designer to help shape and evolve the visual identity of PlanetScale across all touchpoints. In this role, you&#39;ll be a key member of our Marketing team, translating complex technical concepts into compelling visual stories that resonate with developers and technical decision-makers. You&#39;ll craft everything from in-person event experiences to web graphics, merch designs, and creative website assets that make databases feel exciting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What&#39;s the job to be done?&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Visual Brand Development&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design web graphics including technical diagrams, illustrations, and interactive visual assets that simplify complex database concepts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create compelling visual systems for campaigns, product launches, and marketing initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design for multiple formats and contexts: digital, print, experiential, and merchandise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In-Person Experiences&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design booth graphics, signage, and environmental branding for conferences, meetups, and community events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with the events team to create memorable, on-brand experiences that stand out&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design merch that developers actually want to wear and use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create branded collateral including banners, posters, stickers, and promotional materials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Website and Digital Assets&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design creative website components and landing pages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design data visualizations and technical diagrams that make complex information accessible.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create social media graphics, blog post imagery, and other digital marketing assets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop templates and design systems that enable the team to move quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Brand Evolution&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with marketing leadership to evolve and expand the PlanetScale brand identity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Explore new visual directions while maintaining brand coherence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document design decisions and maintain brand guidelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;These attributes best describe you.&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong portfolio demonstrating versatile design skills across digital, print, and experiential design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of design fundamentals: typography, color, composition, and visual hierarchy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve figured out where AI actually helps in a design workflow and built process around it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working in both brand and production modes. You can think big picture and execute in the details.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills with the ability to both articulate design decisions and understand direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-directed and able to manage multiple projects with competing deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative spirit with the ability to incorporate feedback while maintaining creative vision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What else will help you be successful.&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing for technical or developer-focused brands.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Figma, Adobe Creative Suite, and other design tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable using AI to build a working first draft of a page rather than handing off a static mockup.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of design systems and component-based thinking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enthusiasm for learning about databases, infrastructure, and developer tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Why PlanetScale&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re redefining how high-growth companies manage data at scale—and we work with some of the most exciting brands in gaming, consumer tech, and B2B SaaS. As a Brand Designer, you&#39;ll help shape how developers and engineering leaders perceive and interact with PlanetScale, translating the power of our platform into visual experiences that inspire and inform. PlanetScale is a profitable company with a philosophy centered around building small teams of p99 individuals and is recognized as one of the fastest growing companies in America.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At PlanetScale we believe in supporting people to do their best work and thrive no matter the location. Our mission is to build a diverse, equitable, and inclusive company. We strive to build an inclusive environment where all people feel that they are equally respected and valued, whether they are a candidate or an employee. We welcome applicants of any educational background, gender identity and expression, sexual orientation, religion, ethnicity, age, citizenship, socioeconomic status, disability, pregnancy status, and veteran status.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you have a disability, please let us know if there&#39;s any way we can make the interview process better for you; we&#39;re happy to accommodate!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Total Compensation and Pay Transparency&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;An employee&#39;s total compensation consists of base salary + benefits + equity. A member of our Talent Acquisition team will be happy to answer any further questions when we engage with you to begin the interview process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Base salary range:&lt;/strong&gt; $170,000 - $220,000 USD&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;PlanetScale is growing rapidly and reinventing the database space. The PlanetScale platform offers both Postgres and Vitess clusters. Vitess, an open-source database clustering system for horizontal scaling of MySQL, enables businesses to efficiently handle large-scale data workloads — without sacrificing developer experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our customers entrust us with what is often their most precious digital asset, their data, so the stakes couldn’t be higher. We’re looking for a Customer Support Engineer to help developers and businesses get the most out of PlanetScale, resolve issues quickly, and build the support function that helps us scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What’s the job to be done?&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will advise and handle support requests from customers and developers on the PlanetScale platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will respond to, debug, and resolve customer support issues through support tickets, customer Slack channels, public discussions, and other support channels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will help customers understand how to use PlanetScale effectively, including how to reason about queries, schema changes, application behavior, database connectivity, and production workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will create and improve internal and external documentation, support playbooks, troubleshooting guides, and customer-facing materials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will identify product gaps and recurring sources of customer friction, then work with Engineering to prioritize improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will contribute to the systems, processes, and practices that help PlanetScale deliver excellent developer-focused support at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;These attributes best describe you.&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are customer-focused, empathetic, and clear in how you communicate, while knowing when to push back in ways that help customers become successful on their own.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have excellent debugging and troubleshooting skills, with the curiosity and persistence to follow issues across applications, databases, infrastructure, and product behavior.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable stepping outside your comfort zone. Whether that means reading unfamiliar application code, digging into database behavior, testing a new framework, or learning a connector you haven’t used before, you’re willing to go where the problem leads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are a self-starting, enthusiastic individual who takes responsibility for outcomes and wants to make a meaningful impact on the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can operate independently, but you know when to ask for help and how to bring the right people into an issue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are highly organized and able to operate in ambiguous or changing situations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are data-driven, team-oriented, and comfortable communicating across many audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You enjoy working cross-functionally and translating customer pain into actionable product, documentation, and process improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you will need.&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting production applications, databases, developer tools, infrastructure, or other technical products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of SQL, preferably with experience in MySQL and/or PostgreSQL.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong debugging skills and the ability to reason through application and database behavior.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Programming experience. You will not be programming full-time, but you should be comfortable reading and navigating unfamiliar code to understand customer issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with common application frameworks, ORMs, database connectors, or application deployment patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to explore new languages, frameworks, tools, and customer environments as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong empathy for customers, developers, and teammates, with the ability to advocate for customer needs clearly and constructively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What else will help you be successful.&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a remote organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with cloud platforms such as AWS, GCP, or Azure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of monitoring, observability, and debugging tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience helping build support processes, documentation systems, or teams from an early stage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Why PlanetScale.&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re redefining how high-growth companies manage data at scale — and we work with some of the most exciting brands in gaming, consumer tech, and B2B SaaS. As a Customer Support Engineer, you’ll be on the front lines helping developers and businesses solve real production problems, while also shaping the product, documentation, and support systems that make PlanetScale better for every customer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;PlanetScale is a profitable company with a philosophy centered around building small teams of p99 individuals and is recognized as one of the fastest growing companies in America.&lt;/p&gt;
